# API Reference — NB Feedback Kit

## Overview

REST API for NB Feedback Kit, hosted as a Cloudflare Worker (Hono.js). Three authenticated endpoints power feedback collection, release notes, and roadmap display. All authenticated requests require an `X-API-Key` header that maps server-side to a GitHub repository.

**Base URL (production):** `https://nb-feedback-api-prod.<your-subdomain>.workers.dev`
**Base URL (development):** `https://nb-feedback-api-dev.<your-subdomain>.workers.dev`

---

## Authentication

All `/api/*` endpoints require an API key sent in the `X-API-Key` header.

```
X-API-Key: your-api-key
```

API keys are stored in Cloudflare KV (`API_KEYS` namespace) and map to a repository configuration:

```json
{
  "name": "My App",
  "github": { "owner": "my-org", "repo": "my-repo" },
  "rateLimit": 30
}
```

- The client **never** specifies the target repository — it is resolved from the API key (ADR-005).
- Each API key is rate-limited independently by a Durable Object (60-second sliding window).
- Invalid or missing keys return `401`. Rate-limit breaches return `429`.

### Rate Limit Headers

Every authenticated response includes:

| Header                  | Description                              |
| ----------------------- | ---------------------------------------- |
| `X-RateLimit-Limit`     | Max requests allowed per 60s window.     |
| `X-RateLimit-Remaining` | Remaining requests in the current window.|

On `429` responses, `Retry-After` (seconds) is also included.

