## Endpoints

### Health & Info (Public)

#### `GET /`

Returns API metadata and an endpoint directory.

**Response `200`:**
```json
{
  "name": "NB Feedback Kit API",
  "version": "0.0.1",
  "endpoints": {
    "health": "GET /health",
    "feedback": "POST /api/feedback",
    "releases": "GET /api/releases",
    "roadmap": "GET /api/roadmap"
  },
  "documentation": "https://github.com/your-org/nb-feedback-kit"
}
```

#### `GET /health`

Returns service health with a timestamp.

**Response `200`:**
```json
{
  "status": "ok",
  "service": "nb-feedback-api",
  "version": "0.0.1",
  "timestamp": "2026-06-28T14:23:00.000Z"
}
```

---

### Feedback

#### `POST /api/feedback`

Creates a GitHub Issue from user feedback. Issues are auto-labeled based on type (ADR-006):
- `bug` → labels `["bug", "beta-feedback"]`
- `feature` → labels `["feature-request", "beta-feedback"]`
- `feedback` → labels `["feedback", "beta-feedback"]`

**Request body (`FeedbackPayload`):**
```json
{
  "type": "bug",
  "title": "Login button does nothing",
  "description": "Clicking login on /auth has no effect in Safari 17.",
  "metadata": {
    "application": "My App",
    "version": "1.0.0",
    "route": "/auth",
    "browser": "Safari 17",
    "os": "macOS",
    "screenResolution": "1920x1080",
    "timestamp": "2026-06-28T14:23:00.000Z",
    "userId": "user-123"
  }
}
```

**Validation rules:**
- `type` must be one of `bug`, `feature`, `feedback`
- `title` minimum 3 characters
- `description` minimum 10 characters
- `metadata` is required (auto-populated by the SDK)

**Success response `201` (`FeedbackResponse`):**
```json
{
  "success": true,
  "issueUrl": "https://github.com/my-org/my-repo/issues/42",
  "issueNumber": 42,
  "timestamp": "2026-06-28T14:23:00.000Z"
}
```

**Error responses:**

| Status | When                                                    |
| ------ | ------------------------------------------------------- |
| `400`  | Missing required fields, invalid type, or short content |
| `401`  | Missing or invalid `X-API-Key`                          |
| `429`  | Rate limit exceeded                                     |
| `500`  | `GITHUB_TOKEN` not configured on the server             |
| `502`  | GitHub API call failed (bad credentials, repo not found)|

