### Release Notes

#### `GET /api/releases`

Fetches the latest 10 GitHub Releases for the repo mapped to the API key.

**Response `200`:**
```json
{
  "success": true,
  "releases": [
    {
      "version": "v1.2.0",
      "date": "2026-06-20T10:00:00Z",
      "body": "## What's New\n\n- Added dark mode\n- Fixed login bug",
      "url": "https://github.com/my-org/my-repo/releases/tag/v1.2.0"
    }
  ],
  "timestamp": "2026-06-28T14:23:00.000Z"
}
```

**Error responses:** `401`, `429`, `500` (token missing), `502` (GitHub failure).

---

### Roadmap

#### `GET /api/roadmap`

Fetches GitHub Issues labeled `planned`, `in-progress`, or `released`. Status is derived from labels.

**Response `200`:**
```json
{
  "success": true,
  "roadmap": [
    {
      "id": 15,
      "title": "Dark mode",
      "status": "released",
      "url": "https://github.com/my-org/my-repo/issues/15"
    },
    {
      "id": 23,
      "title": "Export to CSV",
      "status": "in-progress",
      "url": "https://github.com/my-org/my-repo/issues/23"
    }
  ],
  "timestamp": "2026-06-28T14:23:00.000Z"
}
```

**Error responses:** `401`, `429`, `500` (token missing), `502` (GitHub failure).

---

## Error Response Shape

All errors return a consistent JSON structure:

```json
{
  "success": false,
  "error": "Human-readable message",
  "timestamp": "2026-06-28T14:23:00.000Z"
}
```

Rate-limit (`429`) responses additionally include:

```json
{
  "retryAfter": "60",
  "resetAt": "2026-06-28T14:24:00.000Z"
}
```

GitHub-failure (`502`) responses additionally include a `details` field with the underlying GitHub error message (server-side only context).

